\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset space \quad{}
\end_inset

The concavity of 
\begin_inset Formula $e(p,x^{*})$
\end_inset

 in 
\begin_inset Formula $p$
\end_inset

 for given 
\begin_inset Formula $x^{*}$
\end_inset

, which is a very important property, is actually fairly intuitive.
 Suppose that we initially have prices 
\begin_inset Formula $\bar{p}$
\end_inset

 and that 
\begin_inset Formula $\bar{x}$
\end_inset

 is an optimal consumption vector at these prices in the EMP.
 If prices change, but we do not let the consumer change her consumption
 levels from 
\begin_inset Formula $\bar{x}$
\end_inset

, then the resulting expenditure will be 
\begin_inset Formula $p\cdot\bar{x}$
\end_inset

, which is a 
\emph on
linear
\emph default
 expression in 
\begin_inset Formula $p$
\end_inset

.
