\begin_layout Subsubsection*
The Hicksian (or Compensated) Demand Correspondence
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset space \quad{}
\end_inset

The set of optimal commodity vectors in the EMP is denoted 
\begin_inset Formula $h(p,x^{*})\subseteq\mathbb{R}_{+}^{L}$
\end_inset

, and is known as the 
\emph on
Hicksian
\emph default
, or 
\emph on
compensated
\emph default
, 
\emph on
demand correspondence
\emph default
, or 
\emph on
function
\emph default
 if single-valued.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset space \quad{}
\end_inset

Three basic properties of the Hicksian demand are given in Proposition 23,
 which parallels Proposition 18 for Walrasian demand.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Proposition*

\series bold
\shape up
(23).

\series default
 
\emph on
Let 
\begin_inset Formula $\succsim$
\end_inset

 be a continuous and locally non-satiated preference relation on 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathbb{R}_{+}^{L}$
\end_inset

.
 Then, for each 
\begin_inset Formula $p\gg0$
\end_inset

, 
\begin_inset Formula $h$
\end_inset

 is:
