\bar under
Part B.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Proof
\begin_inset space \quad{}
\end_inset

This property follows from continuity of 
\begin_inset Formula $\succsim$
\end_inset

.
 We want to prove that 
\begin_inset Formula $\forall\ x\in h(p,x^{*}):x\sim x^{*}$
\end_inset

.
 Suppose 
\begin_inset Formula $\exists\ x^{\prime}\in h(p,x^{*}):\neg(x^{\prime}\sim x^{*})$
\end_inset

.
 Then, 
\begin_inset Formula $\neg(x^{\prime}\succsim x^{*})$
\end_inset

 or 
\begin_inset Formula $\neg(x^{*}\succsim x)$
\end_inset

.
 Since 
\begin_inset Formula $x^{\prime}\succsim x^{*}$
\end_inset

 must be true for 
\begin_inset Formula $x^{\prime}\in h(p,x^{*})$
\end_inset

, then we have 
\begin_inset Formula $\neg(x^{*}\succsim x^{\prime})$
\end_inset

.
 By definition of 
\begin_inset Formula $\succ$
\end_inset

, 
\begin_inset Formula $\left[x^{\prime}\succsim x^{*}\ \wedge\ \neg(x^{*}\succsim x^{\prime})\right]\iff x^{\prime}\succ x^{*}$
\end_inset

.
 Then, 
\begin_inset Formula $x^{\prime}\in U(\succ,x^{*})$
\end_inset

.
 Also, by transitiviy of 
\begin_inset Formula $\succsim$
\end_inset

, 
\begin_inset Formula $x^{\prime}\succ x^{*}\succsim0\implies x^{\prime}\succ0^{*}$
\end_inset

.
 So, 
\begin_inset Formula $x^{\prime}\neq0$
\end_inset

, and since 
\begin_inset Formula $p\gg0$
\end_inset

, then 
\begin_inset Formula $p\cdot x^{\prime}>0$
\end_inset

.
 Now, by Corollary 1, 
\begin_inset Formula $\succsim$
\end_inset

 is continuous if and only if 
\begin_inset Formula $\forall\ x\in X$
\end_inset

, 
\begin_inset Formula $U(\succ,x)$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $L(\succ,x)$
\end_inset

 are open in 
\begin_inset Formula $X$
\end_inset

.
 Since 
\begin_inset Formula $U(\succ,x^{*})$
\end_inset

 is open, then 
\begin_inset Formula $\exists\ \alpha\in(0,1):\alpha x^{\prime}\in U(\succ,x^{*})$
\end_inset

.
 Define 
\begin_inset Formula $x^{\prime\prime}\equiv\alpha x^{\prime}$
\end_inset

.
 Now, 
\begin_inset Formula $x^{\prime\prime}\neq0$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $x^{\prime\prime}\succ x^{*}$
\end_inset

.
 Since 
\begin_inset Formula $x^{\prime}\gneq x^{\prime\prime}$
\end_inset

, then 
\begin_inset Formula $p\cdot x^{\prime\prime}<p\cdot x^{\prime}$
\end_inset

 for 
\begin_inset Formula $p\gg0$
\end_inset

.
 Hence, 
\begin_inset Formula $x^{\prime\prime}\succ x^{*}$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $p\cdot x^{\prime\prime}<p\cdot x^{\prime}$
\end_inset

.
 But this contradicts 
\begin_inset Formula $x^{\prime}\in h(p,x^{*})$
\end_inset

 
\begin_inset Formula $(\rightarrow\leftarrow)$
\end_inset

.
 Thus, 
\begin_inset Formula $\forall\ x\in h(p,x^{*}):x\sim x^{*}$
\end_inset

.
