\end_inset

.
 Suppose that the associated choice correpondence is single-valued and its
 associated demand function is 
\begin_inset Formula $C^{1}$
\end_inset

.
 Then, for each pair 
\begin_inset Formula $(p,w)\in\mathbb{R}_{++}^{L}\times\mathbb{R}_{+}$
\end_inset

,
\end_layout

\begin_deeper
\begin_layout Enumerate
\begin_inset Formula $S(p,w)$
\end_inset

 is symmetric.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
\begin_inset Formula $S(p,w)$
\end_inset

 is negative semi-definite.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
\begin_inset Formula $S(p,w)p=0$
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
The matrix obtained by deleting the 
\begin_inset Formula $l$
\end_inset

-th row and the 
\begin_inset Formula $l$
\end_inset

-th column from 
